## Step 6 — Buyer Spec Audit

### Phase 1 — Top 2 RFQ Specs

**Provided specs:** Length, Width, Application

**Length** (20 ft / 40 ft / 10 ft / 12 ft / 15 ft / 30 ft): Directly determines the product size and price tier. A seller needs to know length to confirm they manufacture that size and to quote accurately. Non-interchangeable across project requirements. **Rank 1.**

**Application** (Office / Residential / Cafeteria / Hospitality / Labor Housing / Storage): Routes the RFQ to sellers who supply the right configuration — a labour housing bunkhouse has different amenity requirements than an office cabin or cafeteria. Sellers need this to determine fit and relevant configuration. **Rank 2.**

*(Width was considered for Rank 2 but Application carries more routing value — width is often standardised at 10 ft for most bunkhouses and is less differentiating than application type.)*

### Phase 2 — Thumbnail Eligibility

**Length** (20 ft / 40 ft / 10 ft / 12 ft / 15 ft / 30 ft): Numeric/dimensional spec — no meaningful visual difference between a "20 ft" and "40 ft" label in a thumbnail. `thumbnail_eligible: false`.

**Application** (Office / Residential / Cafeteria / Hospitality / Labor Housing / Storage): Each application value maps to a visually distinct configuration — a labour housing bunkhouse (rows of bunks, basic finish) looks different from an office cabin (desk, AC, professional finish) or cafeteria (dining tables, kitchen counter). `thumbnail_eligible: true`. `thumbnail_options: ["Office", "Residential", "Labor Housing", "Cafeteria", "Storage"]`

*(Hospitality excluded from thumbnail_options — this is a minority use case for bunkhouses and visually ambiguous; the 5 listed values are the visually distinct primary applications.)*

### Phase 3 — Missing Buyer Spec Audit

**Candidate from Agent 3 vision_output:** Occupancy/Capacity — Agent 3 explicitly identifies occupancy as a primary commercial differentiator (2–4 / 5–8 / 9–16 / above 16 persons). Cross-referencing buyer_spec_list — "Occupancy", "Capacity", "Number of Persons", or semantic equivalent is absent. Sellers need this to confirm they can supply the right-sized unit and to quote accurately. **Confirmed missing.**

**Candidate from LLM world knowledge:** Wall Panel / Insulation Type — buyers in hot climates (Rajasthan, Gujarat) or cold climates (Himachal, J&K) specify PUF/EPS insulation as a requirement. Sellers need this to confirm product suitability. Cross-referencing buyer_spec_list — absent. **Confirmed missing.**

**`would_be_rank` assessment:**
- Occupancy: More important than Application (Rank 2) — occupancy directly determines product size and price, and is a non-interchangeable requirement. `would_be_rank: 2` (displacing Application to Rank 3).
- Wall Panel / Insulation Type: Less important than both Length (Rank 1) and Occupancy (would_be_rank 2) — it is a qualifier after size and capacity are confirmed. No `would_be_rank` assigned.

**Thumbnail eligibility for missing spec with would_be_rank ≤ 2:**
